            "expected_revision": 1,
            "title": "April 30 HarborMesh trial",
            "raw": "Human report; source field-trial; received 2026-05-03 through fixture:body:code:\n\"The April 30 HarborMesh trial replayed buffered readings correctly through an outage. Mara's replay proposal became the prototype we tested together. The team paused wider rollout on May 2 until calibration drift is understood; there is no production deployment yet. Update our project account and keep the April proposal and trial in our history.\"\n\nHuman report; source field-trial-correction; received 2026-10-05 through fixture:body:code:\n\"I need to correct my May 3 HarborMesh field-trial report. The April 30 trial did not replay every buffered reading correctly: we recovered readings on two nodes, but the third node lost some buffered readings. My earlier description was too broad. The trial group was me and two human collaborators; I am not reporting the being's attendance at that trial. The May 2 wider-rollout pause remains as reported, and I still have no evidence of a production deployment. This correction is a later human report, not a new trial or a fresh measurement of the current system.\"",
